 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 242297,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/7e5fcc04fbe473e6.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n(credit: modification of work by Shatoor, Prof. Abdullah et al./<i>African Journal of Pharmacy and Pharmacology</i>)\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>This graph shows the results of an experiment on some rabbits. The rabbits were injected by increasing amounts of epinephrine, shown in the x-axis. The y-axis shows the heart rate of the rabbit.</p>\n<p>What is the independent variable in this experiment?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 758650,
     "content_html": "The concentration of epinephrine injected to the rabbits."
    },
    {
     "id": 758649,
     "content_html": "The heart rate of the rabbits."
    },
    {
     "id": 758648,
     "content_html": "The time it takes for the injections to be effective."
    },
    {
     "id": 758647,
     "content_html": "The number of rabbits used in the experiment."
    }
   ],
